# The files hashed into every run keep their committed bytes on every platform. With `core.autocrlf` on Windows, the prompts and the cards
# would be checked out with CRLF, and prompt_hash and the card's sha256 would no longer match the runs made with them. The split files were
# written by Python's csv module with CRLF and committed that way, so Git leaves their bytes alone.
prompts/** text eol=lf
data/**/*.json text eol=lf
data/**/*.csv -text
